  "environment": "`build` is `none` on purpose. The `.venv` in the clone is the environment every number of plan 2026-11-23 was measured in, and `scripts/field_check.py` cannot rebuild it: `uv sync --frozen --no-install-project` installs the default dependency groups, which for bookwyrm is `dev` only: its runtime dependencies are all in the group `main`, so Django would not be installed. The environment is `uv sync --frozen --no-install-project --only-group main` with the untracked `uv.lock` uv generated from the tracked `pyproject.toml` (Python 3.13.14, Django 5.2.17; this command reports no change on the existing `.venv`). On a clone without that `.venv` the third-party imports are not followed and the counts are different.",
  "oracle": "Django's own resolver, walked by tests/e2e/django_oracle.py in this clone's environment (the controller's run for plan 2026-11-23-python-django-redesign; the walk also calls each view to find its allowed methods). The oracle file itself is a scratch file and is not kept in the repository; the numbers below are the compare of 2026-11-24 (Task 10). ",
